# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_aiera_recall_panel.py" "AIERA PANEL GATE: PASS" "AI-era recall panel (customer-profile measurement harness is honest)" "the AI-era recall panel (tests/aiera_recall_panel.py) pools graph/co-change/COMBINED recall over a PINNED, DOCUMENTED sample of the REAL customer profile (amateur + AI building app/SaaS NOW, 2024-2026 indie repos) across the languages the customer uses (python/javascript/typescript/go), so any future round can re-measure 'where do we stand on the real customer profile and what coupling are we still blind to' with ONE command instead of re-picking an ad-hoc repo set. The numbers themselves come from already-gated tools (84-combined_recall.gate proves the recall LOGIC; recall_measure.py the dampening cost). This gate proves the PANEL HARNESS is honest and safe WITHOUT cloning anything (no git, no Postgres, no network): (1) the PANEL is well-formed and documented -- every entry is (dir, fullName, lang, WHY) with a non-empty rationale, a customer-set language, a dir name equal to fullName-with-slashes-as-underscores (so AIERA_PANEL_ROOT/dir resolves what 'gh repo clone owner/repo' lands), and the sample spans ALL of python/javascript/typescript/go (not one language); (2) pooling is a MICRO-average (sum hits / sum incidents) and NEVER a mean-of-percentages -- proven on a tiny in-memory two-repo fixture where micro (2.0 percent) and macro (about 50 percent) DISAGREE, with the panel source asserted to divide by SUMMED incidents and to use no mean()/statistics; (3) network-free AT RUN TIME -- the panel imports no subprocess/urllib/requests and calls no clone/fetch/HTTP/os.system (it MAY print a one-time clone command as populate guidance, which is documentation, not execution); (4) content-free posture is inherited -- the panel reads no repo file body itself, delegating all repo access to the already-content-free combined_recall/recall_measure analyze(). MEASURED RESULT this harness pins (PINNED 2026-07-20 baseline, current-main extractor, 9 evaluable AI-era repos, 10741 correction-incident pairs): graph-only 16.5 percent, co-change-only 6.5 percent, COMBINED 20.7 percent (micro-avg), dominant miss = no-graph-edge CROSS-DIR (83.6 percent) = cross-tier backend<->frontend contracts + sibling feature-module co-evolution -- the AI-era blind spot a single-language structural graph cannot see. The superseded round6 numbers (13.6/15.8/24.9, 12 repos) are historical only. Honest boundary printed: incident & co-change ground truths are proxies, and the micro-average is a pessimistic view (commit-weighted combined is 54.4 percent on the same corpus)." "the AI-era recall panel harness is honest: a well-formed documented customer-profile sample spanning python/js/ts/go, MICRO-average pooling (sum/sum, never mean-of-percentages, proven on a micro!=macro fixture), network-free at run time (no subprocess/urllib/requests/clone), and content-free (delegates all repo reads). The measured pooled COMBINED recall on this profile is 20.7 percent (pinned 2026-07-20) with an 83.6 percent CROSS-DIR no-edge dominant miss." 20
